      "writtenOn": "2025-06-26T05:17:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, but we\u0027re suppressing the [exceptions](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/17/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/reflect/Field.html#get(java.lang.Object)) from `Field.get()`. But you did make me realize that I mixed up which exception I was still catching. The `IllegalArgumentException` could still be thrown and I should still catch it.\n\n```\nIllegalArgumentException - if the specified object is not an instance of the class or interface declaring the underlying field (or a subclass or implementor thereof).\n```",
      "parentUuid": "67cbc85d_ae2e757a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
